  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The outbuilding, by reason of its combined siting and excessive scale results in an unsympathetic and incongruous form of development that fails to reflect the form and proportion of a typical outbuilding for ancillary use associated with the main dwellinghouse in the locality to the detriment of the visual amenity of the surrounding.  The scheme is contrary to policies D3 and D4 of the London Plan (2021) policies D12.3 and D12.4 of Merton's Local Plan (2024)",
    "Reason : 2 - In the absence of a Flood Risk Assessment, it has not been demonstrated the scheme safeguards the risk of flooding in the locality. The proposal is contrary to, in particular, London Plan (2021) policy SI 13 and Merton Local Plan (2024) policy F15.7",
    "Reason : 3 - The applicant has failed to demonstrate, with a lack of information being provided, that the development would comply with adopted planning policies and that the development would not have a harmful impact on the biodiversity value of the site in conflict with Policy G7 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy O15.2 of Merton's Local Plan (2024)",
    "Reason : 4 - *INFORMATIVE*\r\nPlease ensure that all submitted drawings are provided in PDF format. This helps maintain consistency and ensures compatibility with our digital systems.",
    "Reason : 5 - *INFORMATIVE*\r\nAll drawings must include drawing numbers. This is essential for accurate referencing, version control, and efficient processing of applications.",
    "Reason : 6 - *INFORMATIVE*\r\nApplicants and agents seeking further guidance on preparing applications, include block plans and site context drawings, are encouraged to consult the relevant planning resources. Alternatively the council offers a preapplication advice service."
  ],
